	(text "/\\\npropably gonna replace it with fewer regulators,\n cause for example: the camera's vddaf,\n vdddo and vdda could be all supplied by 3.0V,\n and it could also power the esp32,\n not an ideal solution, but correct with datasheet recommended ranges,\n good enough for a compact system like this i think.\nif i do that i'd have to power the core myself, \ninstead of using the internal ldo in the ov5640, cause 1.5v drop would be kind of tough"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 62.738 86.868 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "3e9111b4-77a9-4a76-973d-b1aa4ae2d378")
	)
	(text "/\\\nupside down on the connector"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 267.97 83.82 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "41009fed-0e04-4ff7-8af7-51a5be2b0b7d")
	)
	(text "ideas:\nbuck-boost from <3v to 5v to make it work of lipo or usb or god's will\nas small as the wroom module\nmostly pins, not many connectors\ncompatible with many sensors (top priority is ov5640)\nno edge connectors and 2 layer pcb so it's easy and cheap to manufarture\nfully solderable by hand (preferably a hand with a soldering iron)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 198.882 151.638 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "7663a9fa-6293-459a-969f-65d3c64c7366")
	)
